CyberSec Env
Copyright 2026 CyberSec Env contributors

This product includes software developed as an OpenEnv environment
(https://github.com/meta-pytorch/OpenEnv, BSD-3-Clause) and trained with
Hugging Face TRL (https://github.com/huggingface/trl, Apache-2.0).

The procedural task families in cybersec_env/tasks/families.py are original.

cybersec_env/data/imported/cweval.jsonl contains tasks derived from CWEval —
"Outcome-driven Evaluation on Functionality and Security of LLM Code
Generation" (Peng et al., 2025), Apache-2.0, https://github.com/Co1lin/CWEval
(commit e9a2a12). Each record reuses a CWEval Python task's specification,
reference solution, insecure variant and pytest module, converted into a
repair task by scripts/import_cweval.py. Changes: the insecure variant is
placed under the task's docstring as the prompt, and timeout decorators are
removed from the tests (the grader enforces its own time limit).

cybersec_env/data/imported/seccodeplt.jsonl contains tasks derived from
SecCodePLT / SeCodePLT — "A Unified Benchmark for Evaluating the Security
Risks and Capabilities of Code GenAI" (Yang et al., 2024), MIT,
https://huggingface.co/datasets/Virtue-AI-HUB/SecCodePLT (gated). Each record
reuses a task's description, setup code, vulnerable and patched function and
test table, converted into a repair task with a generated pytest module by
scripts/import_seccodeplt.py.

CWE identifiers are defined by the MITRE CWE project (https://cwe.mitre.org/).
